    "turn_text": "We should. Part of that problem is that when you talk about antibiotics, say penicillin, or something like Keflex, the cephalosporin, there's a process of manufacturing that when you speak to the drug companies, they're always a little bit afraid that the EPA is going to bust them if ever they have something bad happens. Who wants the bad headline? EPA bust XYZ company because of some leak. China doesn't do that. is probably more practical to think that we're going to near-shore some of this as opposed to re-shore. I'm all about bringing the jobs back to the U.S., but if the company decides they don't want the bad headline risk, it may be that we move it to Brazil or to Mexico. Or during the Cold War, we put these processes in Italy. It was an allied nation that produced her antibiotics. We should do that. There should be a goal to do that. We should have a plan to do that.",
